+// adam: while fast-forwarding (and at normal speed too if set_swap_gate_always(true)), a framebuffer swap is applied
+// at a VI only once the graphics tasks that were in flight when the game called osViSwapBuffer (pending_tasks() = the
+// game's own count at that moment) are done, for at most one normal-speed VI. A VI could otherwise land between the
+// swap and the frame's last tasks reaching the renderer, which showed half-drawn frames (HUD missing or black at 4x+,
+// the 3D scene flickering at 1x on some PCs). At 1x it's a setting: on one PC it also left the game without sound.
+void set_swap_gate(uint32_t (*pending_tasks)());
+void set_swap_gate_always(bool always);
 
